 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? It depends on your riding style. If you' a bit rough with corners, or ride in city potholes, you might go through a tyre in a couple of months. Most tyres have a pressure printed on the sidewall, around 30 or 40 pounds. Lower is smoother, higher is faster but wears faster. You' probably fine, but a tyre pressure gauge is cheap and tells you exactly what it is. Go down a few pounds, but only in the dry. Wet tyres can lose pressure fast.",
